From 470d096b79126e123350415bf6765816c9cd3bec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jatniel <noreply@example.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 23:45:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] Show the system keyboard for the profile name box

The profile picker's name box was a plain drawn rectangle, so no tap on it was
a text-field tap (widgets::Kind::Field, which is what makes the touch layer ask
for the system keyboard) and the title's fields only get the keyboard from such
a tap. Opening New or Rename by tapping a button never asked for it.

The name box is now registered as a text field and has its own typing field,
Field::Profile, which opens the keyboard with its screen like the chat does and
closes it when the box goes (Save, Cancel or Back). Enter saves, as the Save
button does, and a keyboard put away comes back with a tap on the box. Typed
text, backspace and the hardware keyboard keep their existing paths.

